   "title": "About this workflow",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Big detailed upscale. The picture is enlarged with 4x-AnimeSharp, resized to Output size (megapixels: 4 ≈ 2048×2048, 8 ≈ 2900×2900),\ncut into 1024px tiles that are each redrawn at denoise 0.35 guided by the SDXL tile ControlNet, and stitched back.\nDenoise: 0.2 = just sharper, 0.35 = new fine detail, higher may change faces or add things.\nThe prompt should describe the picture in general terms (style, quality); it applies to every tile.\nTile overlap hides the seams (128 is safe).\nFor anime / illustration pictures: 4x-AnimeSharp keeps line art clean.\n\nModel: Illustrious / NoobAI anime checkpoints (not the v-pred ones). Default: Nova Anime XL.\nDefaults: 28 steps, CFG 5.5, euler_ancestral / normal."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
